sentences.l:
The Master said: “The young: going in, then filial;
going out, then deferential;
careful and true to their word;
broadly loving the many,
and drawing close to the humane.
In doing this, having strength to spare,
then use it to learn letters.”

Zixia said: “Esteeming worth in exchange for beauty;
serving father and mother, able to spend all his strength;
serving a lord, able to give over his person;
dealing with friends, speaking and having good faith —
though (they) say not yet learned,
I would certainly call him learned.”

The Master said: “Father alive, observe his intent;
father gone, observe his conduct;
three years without changing from his father's way —
he can be called filial.”

Master You said: “Of the rites' practice, ease counts as most precious.
The former kings' way — this was its beauty;
small and great went by it.

The Master said: “A gentleman, eating, does not seek fullness;
dwelling, does not seek comfort;
quick in affairs and careful in speech;
goes to those who have the Way and is set right by them —
he can be called fond of learning, and that is all.”
